prompts.MaleWalk:
Use case: stylized-concept, production pixel-art sprite animation sheet. Reference image is the APPROVED design: male Mac on left, female Elias on right. Match exactly the chosen character's face, costume, normal healthy athletic proportions, pixel detailing and colors. Fresh coherent drawings, never horizontally squeezed. Actual crisp square-pixel clusters, clean stepped edges, no blur, no painted gradients. This is an animation asset for a right-facing side-scrolling game. ALL frames face RIGHT with the SAME fixed three-quarter side camera, head facing right, no turns and no mirrored character. Completely TRANSPARENT background with real alpha, not black or white and no checker pattern. No ground, no cast shadows, no text, no numbers, no frames or grid lines. Keep every frame wholly inside its evenly spaced cell with transparent gutters. Consistent pixel scale and fixed head size across all cells.
Use ONLY the MALE Mac on the LEFT: black knit beanie, silver hair, brown short leather jacket, white undershirt, shoulder straps with chest pouches, dark charcoal distressed trousers, black combat boots. Healthy normal shoulders and thighs.
WALK BODY LAYER ONLY: exactly EIGHT full-body sprites arranged in FOUR equal columns and TWO equal rows on a wide 3:2 canvas. Both ARMS AND HANDS ARE ABSENT in every frame because separate arm sprites will be attached later. Preserve the complete head, neck, torso, hips, both legs, boots, belt, and coat as ONE CONNECTED shape. Shoulder ends are covered shoulder sockets in clothing, with no dangling sleeve or disconnected accessories. Do not show any guns.
Draw a smooth eight-frame walk cycle, read left to right across row1 then row2:
0 near leg leads forward with heel contact, far leg behind with toe contact;
1 body slightly lowered on planted near leg, far heel lifts;
2 far foot swings forward BEHIND the near planted leg, knees pass each other;
3 body slightly rises, far leg extends forward, near foot begins leaving behind;
4 far leg now leads with heel contact, near leg behind toe contact;
5 body lowered on planted far leg, near heel lifts;
6 near foot swings forward IN FRONT of the planted far leg, knees pass;
7 near leg extends to the next front contact, far foot leaves behind, seamlessly loop into frame0.
Near/far leg identity and shading NEVER swap. The near leg is ALWAYS drawn on top at overlap, even while it is the rearward foot; the far leg always stays behind, even when forward. Both legs have visibly alternating forward/back movement. Pelvis travel is horizontal in place, boots touch a common baseline, maximum body bob only a few pixels. Head, chest width, belts and costume details remain consistent. Cloth follows gait subtly and never hides the crossing knee/boot silhouettes completely. Approximate native full character height 200px, nearest-neighbor integer enlargement for delivery; deliberate dot-art feeling.

